    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e78952a7_9a6ccd51",
        "filename": "java/framework/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 626,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-03T11:25:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we should report this as an error; if we can\u0027t remove the ID, we just can\u0027t.\n\nThe contract for delete() is that it throws if \"if the virtual machine does not exist, is not stopped, or cannot be deleted.\" \n\nThere\u0027s nothing much the app can do to recover if delete fails, so it pretty much never should.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 622,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 626,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "05a7689839931c2cf91e32171f59ac95b4b5ae3a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4fd9d35d_0db35850",
        "filename": "java/framework/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 626,
      "author": {
        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-03T12:30:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But we don\u0027t ignore errors in `deleteRecursively`, why ignore here? - We could argue for allocation of same `id` is unlikely (because it is 64 bytes\u0027 long), so maybe just hoarding id (leaking it like this) is fine.\n\nLets do it as you recommended.",
      "parentUuid": "e78952a7_9a6ccd51",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 622,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 626,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "05a7689839931c2cf91e32171f59ac95b4b5ae3a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "73864a9e_c3f10987",
